{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777090009,"nonce":"E2TFuyH+09ieZDmYwXm7qhjXHyc=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAejeDQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/84","origin":"github"},"title":"record_camera_topics.sh: re-add camera_info topics dropped during scripting","message":"## Problem\n\n`bizzyboat_project11/scripts/record_camera_topics.sh` (introduced on `feature/issue-81` / PR #82) is missing the four `camera_info` topics from its `TOPICS` array. As a result, bags produced by the script have no `camera_info` data — bag-replay rectification, calibration-aware projection, or any other `image_pipeline`-style processing can't run from these bags alone.\n\n## Evidence (bag comparison)\n\n- **Old ad-hoc bags** (e.g. `~/data/logs/bizzy_images/bag_2026-04-21T13.58.31/`): four `oak_\u003cX\u003e/camera_info` topics present at 5 Hz each.\n- **New `record_camera_topics.sh` bags** (e.g. `~/data/logs/bizzy_images/bag_2026-04-24T18.02.04_ffmpeg_seg/`): no `camera_info` topics at all.\n\nThis regression is unintentional — the script was meant to make recording consistent and accidentally dropped `camera_info` while shifting from ad-hoc to scripted capture.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd the four `camera_info` topics to the `TOPICS` array in `bizzyboat_project11/scripts/record_camera_topics.sh`:\n\n```\n/bizzy/sensors/cameras/oak_forward/camera_info\n/bizzy/sensors/cameras/oak_starboard/camera_info\n/bizzy/sensors/cameras/oak_aft/camera_info\n/bizzy/sensors/cameras/oak_port/camera_info\n```\n\n`camera_info` is published as `sensor_msgs/msg/CameraInfo` at the same rate as the image streams (~5 Hz per camera). Recording it adds negligible bag size — `CameraInfo` messages are a few hundred bytes each.\n\n## Sequencing\n\n`feature/issue-81` / PR #82 is currently OPEN with status DIVERGED. This fix should land **after** PR #82 merges (otherwise we're stacking on a branch that may rebase/recreate during merge resolution). Once #82 is on `jazzy`, open a worktree off `jazzy` and apply the fix.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `record_camera_topics.sh` records all four `camera_info` topics in addition to the existing image / segmentation / diagnostics / TF set.\n- A new bag captured with the updated script contains messages on each `oak_\u003cX\u003e/camera_info` topic at the camera's published rate.\n\nPart of #81\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}